{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"mkdir -p build/p1c-r3\nsed -n '1,100p' ../datomworld/src/cljc/dao/host/text.cljc\nrg -n 'defn nfc|Normalizer|icu4j' ../datomworld/{deps.edn,src/cljc/dao/host/text.cljc}\nrg -n 'jolt-toolchain|GAMBIT_PREFIX|CHEZ=' build/p1c-r2/matrix.log | head -25\nsed -n '1,200p' host/gambit/source-loader-test.ss\nsed -n '20,65p' ../datomworld/src/cljc/{dao/space/store.cljc,yin/repl/frontends.cljc}\nrg -n ':jolt|runtime-features' host/chez/reader.ss host/gambit/boot.ss | tail -20\nrg -n '\"'^gambit|''^jolt'\"' ../datomworld/docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-gambit-ffi-stage2.md | head\"","aggregated_output":"(ns dao.host.text\n  \"The host strings of the primitive profile\n   (docs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md §4.2, table A). A host string\n   is a sequence of UTF-16 code units on every host (JVM `String`, JS\n   string, Dart `String`).\n\n   Table A, kind P (§2.4): `unit-count`, `code-unit`, `units->string`,\n   `utf8-encode`, `utf8-decode`, `nfc`. Equal arguments give equal\n   results on every host:\n   - `utf8-encode` refuses an unpaired surrogate `:unpaired-surrogate`\n     instead of substituting (the JVM's `?`, U+FFFD elsewhere), so the\n     bytes of every string it accepts are identical on every host; it\n     returns fresh bytes the caller holds the mutation right to.\n   - `utf8-decode` is strict RFC 3629: an overlong form, an encoded\n     surrogate, a code point above U+10FFFF or a truncated sequence is\n     refused `:invalid-utf8`, never decoded to U+FFFD; a leading BOM is\n     content. It is the decoder of `dao.jing.cbor` (`utf8`), extracted.\n   - `nfc` is Unicode Normalization Form C (`java.text.Normalizer`,\n     `String.prototype.normalize`, the `unorm_dart` package); the profile\n     pins Unicode 16.0 (§2.5).\n\n   Table B, P, no host arm: `code-points`, over `unit-count` and\n   `code-unit` (the private `yin.vm.data` helper, made public here).\n\n   Oracle: `dao.host.text-test` and the text rows of table D, re-asserted\n   by `dao.host.conformance-test`. A refusal throws `ex-info` whose data\n   carries `:dao.host/refusal`, a class keyword, and `:dao.host/entry`.\n   Every reader conditional names `:cljd` first, because the ClojureDart\n   build also reads `:clj`.\"\n  #?@(:cljd [(:require [\"dart:convert\" :as convert]\n                       [\"package:unorm_dart/unorm_dart.dart\" :as unorm])\n             (:import [\"dart:core\" FormatException String]\n                      [\"dart:typed_data\" Uint8List])]\n      :clj [(:import (java.nio ByteBuffer)\n                     (java.nio.charset CharacterCodingException CodingErrorAction\n                                       StandardCharsets))]))\n\n\n(defn- refuse\n  [entry cls detail]\n  (throw (ex-info (str \"dao.host refused: \" entry \" \" (name cls) \" (\" detail \")\")\n                  {:dao.host/refusal cls :dao.host/entry entry :detail detail})))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Code units\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn unit-count\n  \"P. The number of UTF-16 code units of string `s`.\"\n  [s]\n  #?(:cljd (.-length ^String s)\n     :clj (.length ^String s)\n     :cljs (.-length s)))\n\n\n(defn code-unit\n  \"P. The UTF-16 code unit at index `i` of `s`, 0 to 0xFFFF; the caller\n   has checked 0 <= i < `unit-count`.\"\n  [s i]\n  #?(:cljd (.codeUnitAt ^String s i)\n     :clj (int (.charAt ^String s (int i)))\n     :cljs (.charCodeAt s i)))\n\n\n(defn units->string\n  \"P. The host string of the UTF-16 code units `units` (each 0 to\n   0xFFFF), unpaired surrogates included.\"\n  [units]\n  #?(:cljd (let [sb (StringBuffer)]\n             (doseq [u units] (.writeCharCode sb u))\n             (.toString sb))\n     :clj (let [sb (StringBuilder.)]\n            (doseq [u units] (.append sb (char u)))\n            (.toString sb))\n     :cljs (let [a (array)]\n             (doseq [u units] (.push a (.fromCharCode js/String u)))\n             (.join a \"\"))))\n\n\n(defn- high-surrogate?\n  [u]\n  (<= 0xD800 u 0xDBFF))\n\n\n(defn- low-surrogate?\n  [u]\n  (<= 0xDC00 u 0xDFFF))\n\n\n(defn code-points\n  \"P, table B. The code points of string `s` as a vector: a surrogate\n   pair decodes to one code point, an unpaired surrogate is its own.\"\n  [s]\n  (let [n (unit-count s)]\n    (loop [i 0\n           out (transient [])]\n      (if (< i n)\n        (let [u (code-unit s i)\n              v (when (< (inc i) n) (code-unit s (inc i)))]\n../datomworld/src/cljc/dao/host/text.cljc:18:   - `nfc` is Unicode Normalization Form C (`java.text.Normalizer`,\n../datomworld/src/cljc/dao/host/text.cljc:195:(defn nfc\n../datomworld/src/cljc/dao/host/text.cljc:203:     :clj (java.text.Normalizer/normalize ^String s java.text.Normalizer$Form/NFC)\n#!/usr/bin/env gsi-script\n(##include \"boot.ss\")\n(##include \"host-apply.ss\")\n(##include \"source-loader.ss\")\n\n(define (source-check description expected run)\n  (let ((got (with-exception-catcher\n               (lambda (e) (jolt-throwable-message (jolt-unwrap-throw e)))\n               run)))\n    (unless (equal? expected got)\n      (fprintf (current-error-port) \"gambitsourceload: FAIL ~a: expected ~s, got ~s\\n\"\n               description expected got)\n      (exit 1))))\n\n(define (ce src) (jolt-pr-readable (jolt-eval-string src)))\n\n(define (run-byte-rows suite)\n  (let ((rows (call-with-input-file \"test/gambit/unit.edn\"\n                (lambda (port) (jolt-read-string (gambit-read-all port))))))\n    (for-each\n      (lambda (row)\n        (when (eq? (jolt-get row (keyword #f \"suite\")) suite)\n          (let ((label (jolt-get row (keyword #f \"label\")))\n                (source (jolt-get row (keyword #f \"expr\")))\n                (expected (jolt-get row (keyword #f \"expected\"))))\n            (source-check label expected (lambda () (ce source)))\n            (printf \"  ok     ~a\\n\" label))))\n      (seq->list (jolt-seq rows)))))\n\n(define roots '((\"test/gambit/fixtures/source-load\" \".jolt\" \".cljc\")))\n(define args (cdr (command-line)))\n(gambit-install-source-loader!\n  (if (null? args)\n      roots\n      (cons (list (path-expand \"src/jolt\" (car args)) \".jolt\") roots))\n  '(\"clojure.core\" \"jolt.ffi\"))\n(source-check \"backend\" \":gambit\" (lambda () (ce \"(jolt.backend-scheme.session/target)\")))\n(source-check \"loaded dependency and reader feature\" \"42\"\n  (lambda () (ce \"(require '[p1c.source-entry :as entry]) (entry/result)\")))\n(source-check \"caller namespace\" \"user\" chez-current-ns)\n(source-check \"reload refusal\" \"require option is unsupported on the gambit source loader: :reload\"\n  (lambda () (ce \"(require 'p1c.source-entry :reload)\")))\n(source-check \"alias-only missing source\" \"No source for namespace: p1c.absent\"\n  (lambda () (ce \"(require '[p1c.absent :as-alias absent]) (require 'p1c.absent)\")))\n(source-check \"surrogate pair str apply\" \"\\\"😀\\\"\"\n  (lambda () (ce \"(apply str [(char 55357) (char 56832)])\")))\n(source-check \"long source literal through compiler\" \"9000\"\n  (lambda () (ce (string-append \"(count \\\"\" (make-string 9000 #\\x) \"\\\")\"))))\n(run-byte-rows (keyword #f \"core-bytes\"))\n(when (pair? args)\n  (source-check \"load upstream dao.host.bytes\" \"nil\"\n    (lambda () (ce \"(require 'dao.host.bytes)\")))\n  (run-byte-rows (keyword #f \"dao-host-bytes\"))\n  (display \"gambitdaobytes: PASS — upstream Dao byte arrays on native gsi\\n\"))\n(display \"gambitsourceload: PASS — native source loading and compiler string emission\\n\")\n   and `dht:<dir>` stores (yin.repl.store).\"\n  (:require #?@(:cljd [[\"dart:io\" :as dart-io]\n                       [clojure.edn :as edn]])\n            #?(:cljd nil\n               :clj [clojure.edn :as edn]\n               :cljs [cljs.reader :as reader])\n            [clojure.string :as str]\n            [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [dao.jing.file :as jing.file]\n            [dao.space.index :as dao.index]\n            [dao.space.store.fs :as fs]))\n\n\n(def content-name\n  \"The content log's own file name inside a durable store directory.\"\n  \"content.jing\")\n\n\n(def head-name\n  \"The durable root pointer's own file name inside a durable store\n   directory: the versioned record naming the latest published\n   manifest.\"\n  \"HEAD\")\n\n\n(def head-version\n  \"The HEAD record version this store writes and accepts.\"\n  1)\n\n\n(def unsupported-host-text\n  \"The refusal for a durable directory on a host build that cannot open\n   files.  Refusing is the contract: a build without a filesystem is never\n   answered with an in-memory store its caller did not choose.\"\n  (str \"a durable store directory is not supported on this host: opening \"\n       \"the content log needs a filesystem, and this build has none; use \"\n       \"an in-memory store, or run on a host with file support (the JVM, \"\n       \"Node, or Dart)\"))\n\n\n(defn host-file-support\n  \"True when this build can open a file-backed store: the JVM, Node, and\n   Dart can; a CLJS build without `js/require` cannot.\"\n  []\n  #?(:cljd true\n     :cljs (exists? js/require)\nhost/chez/reader.ss:12:;;   sets     -> {:jolt/type :jolt/set :value [...]}        (a FORM, not a set)\nhost/chez/reader.ss:13:;;   #tag frm -> {:jolt/type :jolt/tagged :tag :#tag :form ...}  (NO data reader)\nhost/chez/reader.ss:14:;;   #\"src\"   -> {:jolt/type :jolt/tagged :tag :regex :form \"src\"}\nhost/chez/reader.ss:846:;; plus position, as flat :jolt.error/* keys. Three things follow from that.\nhost/chez/reader.ss:1106:;; reader conditionals: jolt's feature set is {:jolt :clj :default}; the FIRST\nhost/chez/reader.ss:1111:;; :jolt branch placed before :clj.\nhost/chez/reader.ss:1799:;; read-string/read return DATA, so set literal FORMS ({:jolt/type :jolt/set\n6:gambit-ffi-plan.gpt-6-astra.findings.md §2 Callbacks, §3 gate table), the codex\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat > build/p1c-r3/closure.clj <<'EOF'\n(require '[clojure.java.io :as io] '[clojure.string :as str])\n(import '[clojure.lang LispReader\"'$Resolver] '\"'[java.io PushbackReader])\n(def root (first *command-line-args*))\n(def roots [[(str root \\\"/src/jolt\\\") [\\\".jolt\\\" \\\".cljc\\\" \\\".clj\\\"]]\n            [(str root \\\"/src/cljc\\\") [\\\".cljc\\\" \\\".clj\\\"]]\n            [(str root \\\"/src/clj\\\") [\\\".clj\\\"]]\n            [\\\"stdlib\\\" [\\\".jolt\\\" \\\".cljc\\\" \\\".clj\\\"]]\n            [\\\"jolt-core\\\" [\\\".cljc\\\" \\\".clj\\\"]]])\n(defn source [n]\n  (let [path (-> (str n) (str/replace \\\".\\\" \\\"/\\\") (str/replace \\\"-\\\" \\\"_\\\"))]\n    (first (for [[dir suffixes] roots, suffix suffixes\n                 :let [file (io/file dir (str path suffix))]\n                 :when (.isFile file)]\n             file))))\n(defn read-source [file n]\n  (with-open [r (PushbackReader. (io/reader file))]\n    (binding [*default-data-reader-fn* tagged-literal\n              *reader-resolver* (reify LispReader\"'$Resolver\n                                  (currentNS [_] n)\n                                  (resolveAlias [_ s] s)\n                                  (resolveClass [_ _] nil)\n                                  (resolveVar [_ _] nil))]\n      (into [] (take-while #(not= ::eof %))\n            (repeatedly #(read {:read-cond :allow :features #{:jolt} :eof ::eof} r))))))\n(defn require-names [clauses]\n  (for [clause clauses :when (and (seq? clause) (#{:require :use} (first clause)))\n        spec (rest clause) :when (not-any? #{:as-alias} spec)\n        :let [target (if (sequential? spec) (first spec) spec)]\n        :when (symbol? target)]\n    target))\n(defn walk [pending loaded]\n  (if-let [n (first pending)]\n    (if (contains? loaded n)\n      (recur (rest pending) loaded)\n      (let [f (source n)\n            forms (when f (read-source f n))\n            ns-form (first forms)\n            clauses (filter seq? (drop 2 ns-form))\n            deps (if (= '\"'ns (first ns-form))\n                   (require-names clauses)\n                   [])]\n        (recur (concat deps (rest pending)) (assoc loaded n [f forms]))))\n    loaded))\n(def loaded (walk '[yin.repl.main] {'clojure.core [nil nil]}))\n(doseq [[n [f forms]] loaded]\n  (println \\\"NS\\\" n (str f))\n  (let [ns-form (first forms)\n        aliases (into #{} (for [clause (drop 2 ns-form)\n                               :when (and (seq? clause) (= :require (first clause)))\n                               spec (rest clause)\n                               :when (and (vector? spec) (= 'jolt.scheme (first spec)))]\n                           (str (second (drop-while #(not= :as %) spec)))))]\n    (doseq [form (tree-seq coll? seq forms)\n            :when (and (seq? form) (symbol? (first form)))\n            :let [head (first form) role (name head)]\n            :when (and (#{\\\"proc\\\" \\\"call\\\" \\\"defsfn\\\" \\\"scheme\\\" \\\"eval-string\\\" \\\"scheme-proc\\\"} role)\n                       (or (#{\\\"jolt.scheme\\\" \\\"jolt.host\\\"} (namespace head))\n                           (aliases (namespace head))))]\n      (println \\\"SCHEME\\\" n head (if (= role \\\"defsfn\\\") (nth form 2) (second form))))))\nEOF\nsed -i '' 's/(not-any? #{:as-alias} spec)/(or (not (sequential? spec)) (not-any? #{:as-alias} spec))/' build/p1c-r3/closure.clj\nclojure -M build/p1c-r3/closure.clj ../datomworld >build/p1c-r3/closure-baseline.log\nwc -l build/p1c-r3/closure-baseline.log\nrg '\"'^SCHEME'\"' build/p1c-r3/closure-baseline.log\nrg '\"'^NS [''^ ]+ $'\"' build/p1c-r3/closure-baseline.log\n\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
